 alt="Pump.fun PUMP token on a cliff edge representing the $127M insider token unlock and liquidity test ahead."
 decoding="async"
 loading="lazy"
 > </picture></figure><div class="content list-post-grid__content"><div class="eyebrow"> <span>Memecoins</span> <span class="list-post-grid__sentiment list-post-grid__sentiment--bearish"> <i class="fa-light fa-arrow-trend-down" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span>Bearish</span> </span></div><h3>Pump Fun to release $127M of insider tokens worth double PUMP’s recent daily volume</h3><p class="excerpt">The July 12 unlock is large enough to test whether trader demand can absorb insider supply without forcing a deeper repricing.</p><div class="post-meta"> <span class="read"><i class="fa-regular fa-clock"></i>4 days ago</span></div></div> </a></article></div><div class="list-post list-post-grid"><article id="post-546197" class="list-post-grid__card"> <a class="list-post-grid__link" href="https://cryptoslate.com/summer-fi-exploit-shows-ai-automation-now-sits-above-defi-smart-contract-risk/" title="New SummerFi DeFi exploit shows AI automation now sits above smart contract risk"><figure class="cover list-post-grid__cover"> <picture> <source media="(max-width: 767px)" data-srcset="https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/automated-defi-vault-weak-link-alert-768x432.jpg"> <noscript><img
 src="https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/automated-defi-vault-weak-link-alert-768x432.jpg"
 alt="Summer.fi exploit warning highlights hidden risks for automated DeFi vault users following a security breach and emergency response."
 decoding="async"
 loading="lazy"
 ></noscript><img class="lazyload"  src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20210%20140%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' data-src="https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/automated-defi-vault-weak-link-alert-768x432.jpg"
 alt="Summer.fi exploit warning highlights hidden risks for automated DeFi vault users following a security breach and emergency response."
 decoding="async"
 loading="lazy"
 > </picture></figure><div class="content list-post-grid__content"><div class="eyebrow"> <span>Hacks</span> <span class="list-post-grid__sentiment list-post-grid__sentiment--bearish"> <i class="fa-light fa-arrow-trend-down" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span>Bearish</span> </span></div><h3>New SummerFi DeFi exploit shows AI automation now sits above smart contract risk</h3><p class="excerpt">Blockaid estimated about $6 million drained as Summer.fi paused Lazy Summer vaults and investigated the cause.</p><div class="post-meta"> <span class="read"><i class="fa-regular fa-clock"></i>5 days ago</span></div></div> </a></article></div><div class="list-post list-post-grid"><article id="post-545568" class="list-post-grid__card"> <a class="list-post-grid__link" href="https://cryptoslate.com/how-tokenized-stocks-fail-as-collateral-even-when-the-stock-price-does-not-move/" title="How tokenized stocks fail as collateral even when the stock price does not move"><figure class="cover list-post-grid__cover"> <picture> <source media="(max-width: 767px)" data-srcset="https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wrapped-stock-collateral-vault-oracle-failure-768x432.jpg"> <noscript><img
 src="https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wrapped-stock-collateral-vault-oracle-failure-768x432.jpg"
 alt="Tokenized stocks collateral vault illustrating wrapped stock oracle failure risk in DeFi lending protocols"
 decoding="async"
 loading="lazy"
 ></noscript><img class="lazyload"  src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20210%20140%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' data-src="https://cryptoslate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wrapped-stock-collateral-vault-oracle-failure-768x432.jpg"
 alt="Tokenized stocks collateral vault illustrating wrapped stock oracle failure risk in DeFi lending protocols"
 decoding="async"
 loading="lazy"
 > </picture></figure><div class="content list-post-grid__content"><div class="eyebrow"> <span>Tokenization</span></div><h3>How tokenized stocks fail as collateral even when the stock price does not move</h3><p class="excerpt">Edel’s exploit was small, but it hit the next frontier for tokenized equities: credit markets, where 1:1 backing is not enough if wrappers, vaults and exchange rates can be gamed.</p><div class="post-meta"> <span class="read"><i class="fa-regular fa-clock"></i>1 week ago</span></div></div> </a></article></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="disclaimers"><div class="footer-disclaimer footer-disclaimer--ai-usage"><header class="footer-disclaimer__header"> <i class="fa-light fa-robot" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span>AI Usage Disclosure</span></header><p>CryptoSlate may use AI tools to support research, editing, and production workflows. Published articles remain editorially reviewed by our team. Read our full <a href="https://cryptoslate.com/disclaimers/ai-usage-disclaimer/">AI usage disclaimer</a>.</p></div><div class="footer-disclaimer"><header class="footer-disclaimer__header"> <i class="fa-light fa-circle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span>Disclaimer</span></header><p>Our writers' opinions are solely their own and do not reflect the opinion of CryptoSlate. None of the information you read on CryptoSlate should be taken as investment advice, nor does CryptoSlate endorse any project that may be mentioned or linked to in this article. Buying and trading cryptocurrencies should be considered a high-risk activity. Please do your own due diligence before taking any action related to content within this article. Finally, CryptoSlate takes no responsibility should you lose money trading cryptocurrencies. For more information, see our <a href="https://cryptoslate.com/disclaimers/">company disclaimers</a>.</p></div></div></div></div></div></article></div><div class="sidebar right has-sidebar-mentions"><div class="sidebar-sticky"><div cl